## Run one GitLab issue

This project includes the `agent-work` CLI and `work-item-runner` skill for a
human-selected GitLab issue. Set `GITLAB_HOST` and numeric
`GITLAB_PROJECT_ID`, then start with the safe preview:

```bash
agent-work run-issue 123 --mode publish --json
agent-work run-issue 123 --mode publish --apply --json
```

The issue must be open, non-confidential, and labelled `agent::ready`. An
applied run opens or updates an MR, retains its independent Git working copy
with private metadata, reports `awaiting_human`, and stops for human review and
merge. See
[`docs/how-to/run-one-gitlab-issue.md`](docs/how-to/run-one-gitlab-issue.md)
and [`.agents/skills/work-item-runner/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/work-item-runner/SKILL.md).

## Run one filesystem request

This project can also process one trusted producer-delivered JSON request from a
filesystem inbox. Configure `AGENT_WORK_REPOSITORIES_FILE` with the trusted
repository alias allowlist, then start with the safe preview:

```bash
agent-work run-file --path ITEM.json --inbox-root ABS_ROOT --repository ALIAS --mode publish --json
agent-work run-file --path ITEM.json --inbox-root ABS_ROOT --repository ALIAS --mode publish --apply --json
```

See [`docs/how-to/run-one-filesystem-request.md`](docs/how-to/run-one-filesystem-request.md)
for the inbox lifecycle and safe application.
